commit 8b1e1d82b4685a42bcc26fbd4ea8f8ece7d63bd1
Author: poupou97 <nbp85hn@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 30 13:50:31 2026 +0700

    fix(WTM-144): P0 §1 — sample data seeds into production repositories; one source for every screen (ADR-TON-014) (#67)
    
    Founder P0 Regression Audit §1. Kills the parallel demo state that let
    foundational inconsistencies ship while 946+ tests passed.
    
    REAL BUGS FIXED (each regression-locked):
    - Export screen silently exported FIXTURE rows instead of the user's data
      (kSample defaults) → now loads the production repositories.
    - Chat AI answered from SAMPLE customers/products for a real business
      (WorkizenAiContextBuilder sample defaults) → builder defaults are EMPTY;
      the responder rebuilds a data-grounded router per turn from the live repos.
    - Timeline screen showed SAMPLE events in real mode → builds from the live
      repositories + generated opportunities.
    - Reports pipeline sample fallback removed (explicit fixtures in tests).
    - Two dashboards that disagreed (real Home vs pushed demo Home) → the demo
      screen is GONE.
    
    NEW MODEL (ADR-TON-014):
    - SampleDataSeeder: "Xem thử Demo" seeds fixtures INTO the real repositories
      with `sample-` ids (idempotent remove-then-insert; order→customer links
      remapped). Sample rows are ordinary rows: editable, deletable.
    - Repository.deleteByIdPrefix on all five repositories (Drift scoped by
      business, in-memory, sample no-op); model withId/withIds remap helpers.
    - Home: sample banner while samples exist; Get-started "Explore Demo Mode"
      seeds in place; Top Opportunities row now uses the generated provider.
    - More: "Nạp dữ liệu mẫu" + "Xóa dữ liệu mẫu" (confirm dialogs; removal
      keeps user data — tested).
    
    TEST GOVERNANCE (§3, production wiring):
    - test/features/tongtai/p0/: seeder lifecycle (idempotency, link remap,
      sample-only deletion, edit-then-remove) · cross-screen consistency
      (context == repositories) · Opportunity e2e (persisted → Rule Engine →
      context slice) · full ACCEPTANCE scenario (fresh → seed → create → update
      → delete-samples → restart → verify).
    - Home tests rewritten over the real Riverpod wiring (seeded container);
      router/export/reports tests now inject fixtures EXPLICITLY — no silent
      sample defaults remain in lib/.
    
    Docs: ADR-TON-014 + ADR-INDEX + CURRENT-STATUS.
    Evidence: flutter analyze clean; 971/971 tests pass.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

